{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01GJzhNh8qVyFaPwVE7dFrqK","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user wants me to generate detailed predicted experimental results for the \"worst\" tier scenario for every planned experiment in the experiment_plan. Let me carefully go through each planned experiment and generate realistic predictions consistent with the worst-tier narrative.\n\nLet me review the worst tier definition:\n- GRPO doesn't provide recovery advantage over SFT\n- RASP has no advantage or even worse than Standard under GRPO\n- CKA correlation is weak\n- All three original claims need rewriting\n- The narrative reframes as \"Do Reasoning LLMs Need Recovery-Aware Pruning?\" — a negative result paper\n\nKey metric ranges given:\n\n\n- postprune_gsm8k_rasp_1319: [0.27, 0.32]\n- postprune_gsm8k_standard_1319: [0.27, 0.31]\n- postprune_gap_pp: [-1, 3]\n- postprune_gap_p_value_5seed: [0.08, 0.4]\n- post_grpo_gsm8k_rasp: [0.55, 0.63]\n- post_grpo_gsm8k_standard: [0.57, 0.66]\n- grpo_recovery_gap_pp: [-5, 2]\n\nNow I'm looking at the specific metric ranges for the worst-case scenario to assign realistic values that support the negative result narrative. Looking at the performance metrics across these experiments, I can see the unstructured_20_post_grpo results fall in the [0.6, 0.68] range. Now I'm moving through each planned experiment to generate predictions, starting with the full GSM8K evaluations for the baseline and pruned variants, then the recovery experiments, followed by the multi-seed runs and ablation studies across different sparsity levels. Now I'm filling in the detailed results for each planned experiment. For the full GSM8K evaluation with 1319 samples, RASP achieves 0.29 while the standard approach gets 0.28—a negligible gap compared to the dense baseline at 0.76. Plans 002 and 003 are already complete with their actual outcomes, while plan 004 shows that after GRPO recovery, the standard model actually outperforms RASP by 4 percentage points. I'm working through the remaining experiments, including GRASPrune baseline results that show post-pruning performance around 0.08.\n\nThe multi-seed analysis across 5 seeds confirms the gap is just noise—RASP at 0.29 ± 0.03 versus standard at 0.28 ± 0.025 with a p-value of 0.15. The scoring ablation reveals that magnitude and gradient components contribute meaningfully, while the CKA term adds only marginal value, with random scoring dropping to 0.15 as expected.\n\nNow I'm looking at CKA's predictive power for recovery—the mixed-effects model shows a weak relationship (β=0.08, p=0.12) with minimal incremental R² of 0.02, suggesting weight norm and gradient importance are the real drivers. Across different sparsity levels, Standard consistently outperforms RASP whether trained with SFT alone or through the full SFT→GRPO pipeline, and this pattern holds at 25% sparsity where Standard recovers to 0.50 versus RASP at 0.48.\n\nAt 30% sparsity both architectures collapse near zero, making recovery infeasible. The OOD evaluation across MATH-500 and HumanEval shows Standard maintains its advantage with no special benefit for RASP, while the Bonsai baseline recovers from 0.25 to 0.58. CKA itself is internally reliable (split-half ρ=0.92) but this reliability doesn't translate to predicting recovery outcomes, and the metric remains stable across different calibration settings. The α ablation is showing minimal sensitivity—values from 0 through 0.5 all hover around 0.28-0.29.\n\nContinuing through the ablation, higher α values start showing gains, reaching 0.40 at α=4, suggesting α is functioning as an importance scaling mechanism rather than a pure CKA effect. The inference speedup is modest at 1.12x with both approaches achieving identical speedup due to matching sparsity patterns. Unstructured pruning substantially outperforms structured pruning (0.55 post-prune, 0.65 after GRPO), which raises questions about the structured pruning motivation. Finally, the SFT recovery results show Standard actually recovers better than RASP on MATH-500, indicating Standard's recovery isn't simply memorization but reflects genuine capability restoration.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":13279,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":13279},"output_tokens":27,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7505ab55-e481-40a0-9dc6-f07ebf7a7c55","uuid":"e537c447-c74c-471c-a87f-a2dd36c70cb7"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01GJzhNh8qVyFaPwVE7dFrqK","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"```yaml\ntier: worst\nnarrative_guidance: >\n  完全reframe为\"Do Reasoning LLMs Need Recovery-Aware Pruning?\"——controlled empirical study，\n  核心发现是surprising negative result：CKA functional overlap不预测RLVR recoverability，\n  但α-scaled importance scoring确实优于vanilla magnitude pruning（与CKA理论联系薄弱），\n  SFT recovery对所有pruning方法都surprisingly effective。\n  GRPO未能逆转Standard在SFT阶段建立的优势，RASP在GRPO下无额外增益甚至略劣。\n  论文价值在于：(1)实验thoroughness本身（5-seed, 3 sparsity, 4 methods, 2 recovery paradigms），\n  (2)α scoring作为简单有效的pruning改进的positive takeaway，\n  (3)对recovery-aware pruning直觉假设的empirically grounded challenge。\n\nimagined_experiments:\n  - name: \"Full GSM8K Eval N=1319 (Post-Prune)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_001\"\n    description: \"Dense baseline + RASP_20 + Standard_20 在完整1319样本上的post-prune评估\"\n    expected_results:\n      dense_baseline_gsm8k_1319: 0.764\n      dense_baseline_ci95: \"±0.023\"\n      rasp_20_gsm8k_1319: 0.293\n      rasp_20_ci95: \"±0.025\"\n      standard_20_gsm8k_1319: 0.281\n      standard_20_ci95: \"±0.025\"\n      rasp_vs_standard_gap_pp: 1.2\n      gap_p_value_bootstrap: 0.34\n      n_samples: 1319\n    result_rationale: >\n      N=100时观测到31% vs 27%（4pp gap），但bootstrap CI为±9pp。\n      扩展到N=1319后CI缩至±2.5pp，真实gap收缩到~1.2pp，\n      因为N=100的4pp gap本身就在seed方差范围内（reeval_postprune_definitive已显示）。\n      RASP的CKA加权在20% sparsity下只重排了少量边界MLP groups，\n      大部分pruning决策与Standard一致（两者共享~85%的pruned set），\n      导致full eval下gap不显著。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 1: Post-Prune GSM8K Accuracy (N=1319)\"\n        columns: [\"Model\", \"Accuracy\", \"95% CI\", \"vs Dense Drop\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Dense Baseline\", \"76.4%\", \"±2.3pp\", \"—\"]\n          - [\"RASP-20\", \"29.3%\", \"±2.5pp\", \"-47.1pp\"]\n          - [\"Standard-20\", \"28.1%\", \"±2.5pp\", \"-48.3pp\"]\n          - [\"Δ (RASP − Standard)\", \"+1.2pp\", \"\", \"p=0.34\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Bar chart: 三个模型的GSM8K accuracy with error bars，视觉上RASP和Standard几乎无法区分\"\n    analysis: >\n      核心发现：原始29% vs 1%的29x优势不可复现（已在reeval_postprune_definitive确认），\n      full eval进一步确认gap仅~1pp且不显著。\n      这直接摧毁了Claim 1的基础——RASP并未在post-prune阶段提供qualitatively different的保留。\n      两种pruning方法都将模型从76%打到~29%，损失相似。\n      论文中需reframe为：在moderate sparsity下，CKA-aware reranking对post-prune accuracy影响有限。\n\n  - name: \"SFT Warmup Recovery\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_002\"\n    description: \"SFT teacher-forcing恢复RASP_20和Standard_20的基本生成能力\"\n    expected_results:\n      sft_rasp_20_gsm8k_100: 0.57\n      sft_standard_20_gsm8k_100: 0.64\n      sft_gap_pp: -7\n      sft_rasp_train_loss_final: 0.64\n      sft_standard_train_loss_final: 0.64\n      sft_rasp_token_accuracy: 0.83\n      sft_standard_token_accuracy: 0.83\n      eos_rate_both: 0.99\n      total_steps: 1870\n    result_rationale: >\n      已完成实验（DONE）。Standard在SFT后反超RASP 7pp（64% vs 57%）。\n      这在worst档下的解释：RASP保护了functionally unique但SFT-unfriendly的structures，\n      而Standard保留了对teacher-forcing更responsive的structures。\n      两者train loss和token accuracy完全相同（0.64, 83%），\n      说明差异不在optimization landscape而在pruned model的representational capacity分配上。\n      关键是：SFT recovery本身extremely effective——从29%→57%/64%，恢复了大部分能力。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 2: SFT Recovery Results\"\n        columns: [\"Pruned Model\", \"Post-Prune\", \"Post-SFT\", \"Recovery Gain\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"RASP-20\", \"29%\", \"57%\", \"+28pp\"]\n          - [\"Standard-20\", \"28%\", \"64%\", \"+36pp\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Training loss curves: 两条曲线几乎完全重合，最终都收敛到0.64\"\n    analysis: >\n      Standard的SFT recovery优势（+36pp vs +28pp）是worst档的关键evidence：\n      recovery更多取决于training signal（SFT data）而非pruning structure。\n      Standard保留的structures虽然CKA overlap更高，但对SFT的gradient信号更receptive。\n\n  - name: \"GRPO Stage-2 Recovery\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_003\"\n    description: \"在SFT-warmed模型上运行GRPO reinforcement learning恢复\"\n    expected_results:\n      grpo_rasp_20_gsm8k_100: 0.59\n      grpo_standard_20_gsm8k_100: 0.63\n      grpo_rasp_vs_sft_gain_pp: 2\n      grpo_standard_vs_sft_gain_pp: -1\n      grpo_gap_pp: -4\n      grpo_rasp_reward_mean_final: 0.42\n      grpo_standard_reward_mean_final: 0.45\n      training_stable: true\n      convergence_step: 800\n    result_rationale: >\n      已完成（DONE, conclusion: negative）。GRPO未能逆转SFT阶段Standard的优势。\n      RASP从57%→59%（+2pp marginal gain），Standard从64%→63%（-1pp，轻微regression）。\n      GRPO在两个模型上的增益都很小，说明SFT已经capture了大部分recoverable performance，\n      GRPO的RL信号在moderate sparsity下缺乏足够的capacity来进一步优化。\n      这与\"GRPO对pruned模型的恢复效果不稳定\"的核心假设一致。\n      Standard的轻微regression可能是GRPO的exploration noise覆盖了SFT学到的patterns。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 3: GRPO Recovery Results\"\n        columns: [\"Model\", \"Post-SFT\", \"Post-GRPO\", \"GRPO Gain\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"RASP-20\", \"57%\", \"59%\", \"+2pp\"]\n          - [\"Standard-20\", \"64%\", \"63%\", \"-1pp\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"GRPO reward curves: 两条曲线都plateau早（~step 800），RASP略低于Standard\"\n      - \"GSM8K accuracy over GRPO steps: 几乎flat，偶尔spike但不稳定\"\n    analysis: >\n      GRPO作为recovery method的added value可疑——SFT alone已达到comparable或更好的结果。\n      这是worst档的decisive evidence：sft_vs_grpo_interaction_significant = False。\n      无论pruning方法如何，GRPO都不提供超过SFT的显著恢复。\n      论文需要reframe：recovery robustness来自training signal（SFT data quality），\n      而非pruning-recovery的structural alignment。\n\n  - name: \"Full GSM8K Eval N=1319 (All Recovered Models)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_004\"\n    description: \"所有recovered模型在完整1319样本上的最终评估\"\n    expected_results:\n      dense_baseline_1319: 0.764\n      sft_rasp_20_1319: 0.553\n      sft_standard_20_1319: 0.635\n      grpo_rasp_20_1319: 0.578\n      grpo_standard_20_1319: 0.621\n      sft_rasp_ci95: \"±0.027\"\n      sft_standard_ci95: \"±0.026\"\n      grpo_rasp_ci95: \"±0.027\"\n      grpo_standard_ci95: \"±0.026\"\n      grpo_vs_sft_rasp_diff: 2.5\n      grpo_vs_sft_standard_diff: -1.4\n      best_overall: \"SFT-Standard (63.5%)\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      N=1319会轻微调整N=100的点估计（regression to mean效应）。\n      SFT Standard的64%可能微降至63.5%，SFT RASP的57%降至55.3%。\n      GRPO模型的full eval同样显示Standard优势持续。\n      关键发现：best recovered model是SFT-only Standard（63.5%），不需要GRPO也不需要RASP。\n      这是worst档最damaging的result——最简单的pipeline（Standard pruning + SFT）给出最好结果。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 4: Full Pipeline Comparison (N=1319)\"\n        columns: [\"Pipeline\", \"Post-Prune\", \"Post-Recovery\", \"Recovery Rate\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"RASP + SFT\", \"29.3%\", \"55.3%\", \"55.4%\"]\n          - [\"RASP + SFT→GRPO\", \"29.3%\", \"57.8%\", \"60.7%\"]\n          - [\"Standard + SFT\", \"28.1%\", \"63.5%\", \"73.0%\"]\n          - [\"Standard + SFT→GRPO\", \"28.1%\", \"62.1%\", \"70.1%\"]\n          - [\"Dense (no pruning)\", \"—\", \"76.4%\", \"—\"]\n        note: \"Recovery Rate = (post_recovery - post_prune) / (dense - post_prune)\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Grouped bar chart: 4 pipelines的post-prune → post-SFT → post-GRPO三阶段accuracy\"\n      - \"Recovery rate scatter: x=post-prune, y=recovery rate, 标注每个pipeline\"\n    analysis: >\n      Paper Table 1的核心数据。Worst档的narrative：Standard+SFT是Pareto optimal——\n      比所有其他pipeline更简单且更好。RASP的CKA-aware pruning反而hurt了SFT recovery。\n      GRPO在两种pruning上的marginal/negative contribution质疑了RLVR recovery的必要性\n      （至少在moderate sparsity下）。\n\n  - name: \"GRASPrune Baseline 20%\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_005\"\n    description: \"GRASPrune（ACL 2026 SOTA）在20% sparsity下的完整pipeline：prune→eval→SFT→GRPO\"\n    expected_results:\n      grasp_20_postprune_gsm8k_100: 0.08\n      grasp_20_postprune_gsm8k_1319: 0.072\n      grasp_20_eos_rate: 0.02\n      grasp_20_post_sft_gsm8k_100: 0.58\n      grasp_20_post_sft_gsm8k_1319: 0.56\n      grasp_20_post_grpo_gsm8k_100: 0.57\n      grasp_20_post_grpo_gsm8k_1319: 0.55\n      grasp_sft_recovery_gain_pp: 50\n      grasp_grpo_additional_gain_pp: -1\n    result_rationale: >\n      GRASPrune的post-prune accuracy极低（8%，已从grasp_baseline_westd观测到），\n      因为它优化的是budgeted pruning的immediate loss而非reasoning preservation。\n      但SFT recovery将其从8%拉到~58%（+50pp），这是worst档最重要的evidence之一：\n      post-prune accuracy与recovery outcome的correlation远低于预期。\n      GRASPrune post-prune最差（8%）但recovery后与RASP（57.8%）comparable。\n      这直接反驳了\"RASP preserves recoverable structures\"的claim——\n      即使post-prune被摧毁到8%，SFT也能恢复到相似水平。\n      GRPO对GRASPrune同样无额外增益（-1pp regression）。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 5: GRASPrune Pipeline Results\"\n        columns: [\"Stage\", \"Accuracy\", \"Gain from Previous\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Post-Prune\", \"7.2%\", \"-69.2pp from dense\"]\n          - [\"Post-SFT\", \"56.0%\", \"+48.8pp\"]\n          - [\"Post-SFT→GRPO\", \"55.0%\", \"-1.0pp\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Recovery trajectory plot: GRASPrune vs RASP vs Standard的三阶段accuracy变化，GRASPrune呈V形恢复\"\n    analysis: >\n      GRASPrune的V形恢复是worst档的smoking gun：post-prune accuracy几乎不预测recovery outcome。\n      8%→56%的恢复意味着SFT的training signal足以重建大部分reasoning ability，\n      regardless of which structures were pruned。\n      这对所有recovery-aware pruning方法（包括RASP）都是existential challenge：\n      如果recovery主要由training data驱动，优化pruning structure的marginal value极小。\n\n  - name: \"Multi-Seed Post-Prune Eval (5 Seeds)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_006\"\n    description: \"5个random seeds下RASP_20和Standard_20的post-prune GSM8K评估\"\n    expected_results:\n      rasp_20_seed42: 0.293\n      rasp_20_seed123: 0.285\n      rasp_20_seed456: 0.301\n      rasp_20_seed789: 0.278\n      rasp_20_seed1024: 0.289\n      rasp_20_mean: 0.289\n      rasp_20_std: 0.008\n      standard_20_seed42: 0.281\n      standard_20_seed123: 0.275\n      standard_20_seed456: 0.292\n      standard_20_seed789: 0.269\n      standard_20_seed1024: 0.283\n      standard_20_mean: 0.280\n      standard_20_std: 0.008\n      pairwise_gap_mean_pp: 0.9\n      pairwise_gap_std: 0.6\n      paired_t_test_p: 0.15\n      wilcoxon_p: 0.19\n      cohens_d: 0.35\n    result_rationale: >\n      5-seed评估下，RASP和Standard的均值gap约0.9pp，标准差~0.8pp。\n      Paired t-test p=0.15，Wilcoxon p=0.19——均不达显著性阈值（p<0.05）。\n      Cohen's d=0.35属于small effect size。\n      seed-to-seed的方差（~0.8pp std）与gap本身（0.9pp）同量级，\n      说明观测到的gap完全可以被eval noise解释。\n      Worst档的关键：5-seed的power不足以detect <1pp的真实差异，\n      但这恰恰说明即使存在真实差异也太小to be practically meaningful。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 6: Multi-Seed Post-Prune Results\"\n        columns: [\"Seed\", \"RASP-20\", \"Standard-20\", \"Δ\"]\n        rows:\n          - [42, \"29.3%\", \"28.1%\", \"+1.2pp\"]\n          - [123, \"28.5%\", \"27.5%\", \"+1.0pp\"]\n          - [456, \"30.1%\", \"29.2%\", \"+0.9pp\"]\n          - [789, \"27.8%\", \"26.9%\", \"+0.9pp\"]\n          - [1024, \"28.9%\", \"28.3%\", \"+0.6pp\"]\n          - [\"Mean±Std\", \"28.9±0.8%\", \"28.0±0.8%\", \"+0.9±0.6pp\"]\n          - [\"p-value\", \"\", \"\", \"0.15 (paired-t)\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Paired dot plot: 每个seed一条线连接RASP和Standard，几乎所有线都近乎水平\"\n      - \"Box plot: RASP和Standard的5-seed分布高度重叠\"\n    analysis: >\n      Post-prune gap在统计上不显著（p=0.15），effect size小（d=0.35）。\n      论文中应honest report这个null result，\n      并argue这个negative finding本身有价值：\n      在moderate sparsity下CKA reranking不改变pruning outcome。\n\n  - name: \"Scoring Ablation at 20% Sparsity\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_007\"\n    description: \"magnitude-only, gradient-only, random pruning对比RASP/Standard\"\n    expected_results:\n      magnitude_only_gsm8k_100: 0.27\n      gradient_only_gsm8k_100: 0.26\n      random_pruning_gsm8k_100: 0.14\n      rasp_alpha4_gsm8k_100: 0.40\n      standard_alpha0_gsm8k_100: 0.28\n      rasp_alpha1_gsm8k_100: 0.30\n      magnitude_only_gsm8k_1319: 0.265\n      gradient_only_gsm8k_1319: 0.255\n      random_pruning_gsm8k_1319: 0.135\n    result_rationale: >\n      Random pruning大幅劣于所有structured方法（14% vs 26-40%），证明pruning order matters。\n      Magnitude-only（27%）≈ Standard（28%）≈ Gradient-only（26%），\n      三种importance-based方法在moderate sparsity下几乎等价。\n      RASP α=4（40%）显著优于所有α=0方法——但这主要是α scaling的效果，不是CKA。\n      关键ablation：α=1（CKA权重较弱）只给30%，仅比Standard好2pp。\n      α=4的大幅提升（+12pp over Standard）更可能是importance distribution的reshaping效应\n      （α放大了high-overlap groups的penalty，但也放大了importance的tail），\n      而非CKA functional overlap的predictive value。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 7: Scoring Ablation (N=100, 20% Sparsity)\"\n        columns: [\"Scoring Method\", \"Post-Prune GSM8K\", \"vs Standard Δ\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Random\", \"14%\", \"-14pp\"]\n          - [\"Gradient-only\", \"26%\", \"-2pp\"]\n          - [\"Magnitude-only\", \"27%\", \"-1pp\"]\n          - [\"Standard (Wanda I(h))\", \"28%\", \"—\"]\n          - [\"RASP α=1.0\", \"30%\", \"+2pp\"]\n          - [\"RASP α=4.0\", \"40%\", \"+12pp\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Bar chart: 6种scoring方法的post-prune accuracy，α=4.0是clear outlier\"\n      - \"Decomposition plot: 将α=4.0的12pp gain分解为importance-scaling vs CKA-specific贡献\"\n    analysis: >\n      α=4.0的优势（+12pp）是worst档的positive takeaway，但解释需要carefully nuanced。\n      α scaling本质上改变了importance score的distribution shape——\n      它upweight了already-important structures并downweight了marginal ones，\n      CKA项(1-F(h))只是这个rescaling的vehicle之一。\n      为证明这一点：可以test α-scaled magnitude-only（I(h)^α without CKA），\n      如果效果similar则CKA的独立贡献为零。\n      论文中应将此framed为\"α-scaled importance scoring improves pruning\"而非\"CKA predicts recoverability\"。\n\n  - name: \"CKA-Recoverability Correlation Analysis\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_008\"\n    description: \"Per-structure CKA F(h)与post-recovery accuracy retention的mixed-effects regression\"\n    expected_results:\n      n_mlp_groups: 784\n      n_pruned_mlp_groups: 200\n      cka_beta_coefficient: 0.08\n      cka_beta_p_value: 0.12\n      cka_incremental_r2: 0.018\n      weight_norm_beta: 0.23\n      weight_norm_p: 0.001\n      gradient_importance_beta: 0.31\n      gradient_importance_p: 0.0003\n      activation_magnitude_beta: 0.19\n      activation_magnitude_p: 0.004\n      full_model_r2: 0.34\n      model_without_cka_r2: 0.32\n      layer_random_effect_variance: 0.15\n      cka_spearman_with_recoverability: 0.11\n      cka_spearman_p: 0.09\n    result_rationale: >\n      Mixed-effects regression显示CKA β=0.08 (p=0.12)，不达显著性。\n      Incremental R²仅0.018（1.8%），远低于useful predictor的阈值（通常>5%）。\n      相比之下weight norm（β=0.23, p=0.001）和gradient importance（β=0.31, p=0.0003）\n      都是stronger predictors。\n      CKA functional overlap与recoverability的Spearman ρ=0.11（p=0.09），borderline但不显著。\n      核心问题：CKA measures inter-head functional similarity，\n      但RLVR recovery不是通过\"redistribute function across heads\"实现的——\n      RLVR更多是global optimization of the loss landscape，\n      individual head的functional overlap对global recovery的predictive power有限。\n      Layer random effect variance (0.15)较大，说明per-layer差异比per-head CKA更重要。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 8: Mixed-Effects Regression Results (MLP Groups, N=784)\"\n        columns: [\"Predictor\", \"β\", \"SE\", \"p-value\", \"Incremental R²\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Gradient Importance\", \"0.31\", \"0.06\", \"<0.001\", \"0.14\"]\n          - [\"Weight Norm\", \"0.23\", \"0.05\", \"0.001\", \"0.09\"]\n          - [\"Activation Magnitude\", \"0.19\", \"0.05\", \"0.004\", \"0.06\"]\n          - [\"CKA Overlap F(h)\", \"0.08\", \"0.05\", \"0.12\", \"0.018\"]\n          - [\"Full Model R²\", \"\", \"\", \"\", \"0.34\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Scatter plot: F(h) vs per-head recoverability，大量scatter，弱correlation线\"\n      - \"Coefficient plot: 4个predictor的β with 95% CI，CKA的CI跨零\"\n      - \"Partial regression plot: 控制其他变量后CKA的residual effect\"\n    analysis: >\n      这是Claim 2的直接否定。CKA functional overlap不是recoverability的significant predictor。\n      Traditional importance metrics（gradient, weight norm）解释了大部分variance。\n      论文reframe：functional overlap是一个intuitively appealing but empirically unsupported\n      predictor of recovery outcomes。\n      Positive spin：实验thoroughness（N=784, mixed-effects, covariates控制）使这个negative\n      result credible且publishable。\n\n  - name: \"SFT-Only Recovery Comparison\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_009\"\n    description: \"Same pruned models, same data budget, SFT-only recovery（无GRPO）\"\n    expected_results:\n      sft_only_rasp_20_gsm8k_100: 0.57\n      sft_only_rasp_20_gsm8k_1319: 0.553\n      sft_only_standard_20_gsm8k_100: 0.64\n      sft_only_standard_20_gsm8k_1319: 0.635\n      sft_only_gap_pp: -7\n      grpo_rasp_20_gsm8k_1319: 0.578\n      grpo_standard_20_gsm8k_1319: 0.621\n      interaction_f_test_p: 0.41\n      pruning_method_main_effect_p: 0.03\n      recovery_method_main_effect_p: 0.62\n      interaction_effect_size: 0.02\n    result_rationale: >\n      plan_002已完成SFT-only recovery（RASP 57%, Standard 64%）。\n      2×2 ANOVA (pruning × recovery)显示：\n      pruning method有main effect（Standard > RASP, p=0.03），\n      recovery method无main effect（SFT ≈ SFT→GRPO, p=0.62），\n      交互作用不显著（p=0.41）。\n      这意味着：Standard在两种recovery下都优于RASP，\n      且recovery method的选择不改变pruning方法的相对排名。\n      Claim 3（recovery method conditions optimal pruning order）被直接否定。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 9: 2×2 Recovery Comparison (N=1319)\"\n        columns: [\"\", \"SFT-Only\", \"SFT→GRPO\", \"Δ(GRPO−SFT)\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"RASP-20\", \"55.3%\", \"57.8%\", \"+2.5pp\"]\n          - [\"Standard-20\", \"63.5%\", \"62.1%\", \"-1.4pp\"]\n          - [\"Δ(Std−RASP)\", \"+8.2pp\", \"+4.3pp\", \"\"]\n      - name: \"Table 10: 2×2 ANOVA Results\"\n        columns: [\"Effect\", \"F\", \"p-value\", \"η²\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Pruning Method\", \"5.12\", \"0.03\", \"0.08\"]\n          - [\"Recovery Method\", \"0.24\", \"0.62\", \"0.004\"]\n          - [\"Interaction\", \"0.68\", \"0.41\", \"0.02\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Interaction plot: pruning method × recovery method，两条线近乎平行（无交互）\"\n    analysis: >\n      Standard在两种recovery下一致优于RASP，GRPO不改变这个ranking。\n      Interaction plot的平行线直接visualize了null interaction。\n      论文reframe为positive finding：SFT recovery is surprisingly robust——\n      无论pruning structure如何，SFT都能恢复到similar relative levels。\n      这暗示recovery robustness更多来自training signal而非pruning structure。\n\n  - name: \"25% Sparsity RASP + Standard\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_010\"\n    description: \"25% sparsity下完整pipeline：prune→eval→SFT→GRPO\"\n    expected_results:\n      rasp_25_postprune_gsm8k_100: 0.18\n      rasp_25_postprune_gsm8k_1319: 0.172\n      standard_25_postprune_gsm8k_100: 0.16\n      standard_25_postprune_gsm8k_1319: 0.155\n      postprune_gap_25_pp: 1.7\n      rasp_25_post_sft_100: 0.48\n      standard_25_post_sft_100: 0.52\n      rasp_25_post_grpo_100: 0.49\n      standard_25_post_grpo_100: 0.53\n      rasp_25_post_grpo_1319: 0.475\n      standard_25_post_grpo_1319: 0.515\n      recovery_rate_rasp_25: 0.512\n      recovery_rate_standard_25: 0.590\n    result_rationale: >\n      25% sparsity下两种方法都受到更大损伤（17-18% post-prune vs 28-29% at 20%）。\n      RASP仍然略优于Standard在post-prune（+1.7pp），但gap依然不显著。\n      SFT recovery将两者提升到48-52%，Standard再次优于RASP。\n      GRPO在25% sparsity下同样无额外增益（+1pp for RASP, +1pp for Standard）。\n      关键观察：从20%到25%，recovery ceiling从~63%降到~53%（-10pp），\n      说明sparsity对recovery outcome的影响远大于pruning method的影响。\n      这进一步support了worst档的narrative：pruning structure的精细选择\n      相比sparsity ratio本身是second-order effect。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 11: 25% Sparsity Pipeline\"\n        columns: [\"Model\", \"Post-Prune\", \"Post-SFT\", \"Post-GRPO\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"RASP-25\", \"17.2%\", \"48%\", \"49%\"]\n          - [\"Standard-25\", \"15.5%\", \"52%\", \"53%\"]\n          - [\"Δ (RASP−Std)\", \"+1.7pp\", \"-4pp\", \"-4pp\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Sparsity × accuracy curve: 20% and 25%下RASP和Standard的recovery trajectories\"\n      - \"Recovery ceiling plot: sparsity ratio vs best-recovered accuracy\"\n    analysis: >\n      25% sparsity数据确认20%的pattern scales：Standard consistently recovers better，\n      GRPO consistently unhelpful。Sparsity ratio是dominant factor。\n      论文中这作为robustness check，strengthen negative findings的generality。\n\n  - name: \"30% Sparsity Probe\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_011\"\n    description: \"30% sparsity下prune + eval only（无recovery），mapping collapse threshold\"\n    expected_results:\n      rasp_30_postprune_gsm8k_100: 0.05\n      standard_30_postprune_gsm8k_100: 0.04\n      rasp_30_eos_rate: 0.15\n      standard_30_eos_rate: 0.08\n      rasp_30_avg_len: 3200\n      standard_30_avg_len: 3800\n      gap_pp: 1\n    result_rationale: >\n      30% sparsity下两种方法都near-collapse（5% vs 4%），\n      consistent with已知的35% sparsity完全collapse（D005）。\n      RASP的marginal advantage缩小到1pp（在noise范围内）。\n      EOS rate大幅下降说明模型生成能力严重受损。\n      不做recovery是正确决策——从5%恢复的cost-benefit不合理。\n      这个data point完成了sparsity response curve：20%(29%)→25%(17%)→30%(5%)→35%(~0%)。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 12: 30% Sparsity Probe\"\n        columns: [\"Model\", \"Post-Prune\", \"EOS Rate\", \"Avg Length\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"RASP-30\", \"5%\", \"15%\", \"3200\"]\n          - [\"Standard-30\", \"4%\", \"8%\", \"3800\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Sparsity response curve: 0-35% sparsity下的post-prune accuracy for RASP和Standard\"\n    analysis: >\n      30% sparsity是\"no man's land\"——pruning too aggressive for meaningful recovery。\n      两种方法无差异。curve shape（smooth degradation 20-25%, cliff 25-30%）\n      suggests a phase transition around 27-28% sparsity for this model。\n\n  - name: \"OOD Evaluation (MATH-500, HumanEval)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_012\"\n    description: \"Best recovered models在MATH-500和HumanEval上的OOD泛化评估\"\n    expected_results:\n      dense_math500: 0.52\n      dense_humaneval: 0.58\n      grpo_rasp_20_math500: 0.24\n      grpo_rasp_20_humaneval: 0.31\n      grpo_standard_20_math500: 0.28\n      grpo_standard_20_humaneval: 0.35\n      sft_standard_20_math500: 0.30\n      sft_standard_20_humaneval: 0.37\n      rasp_math500_advantage_pp: -4\n      rasp_humaneval_advantage_pp: -4\n      math500_recovery_rate_rasp: 0.36\n      math500_recovery_rate_standard: 0.46\n    result_rationale: >\n      OOD eval显示RASP在MATH-500和HumanEval上均劣于Standard（-4pp each）。\n      Standard的OOD优势与GSM8K上的优势consistent——\n      不是GSM8K-specific pattern memorization而是genuine reasoning recovery。\n      RASP的OOD劣势可能因为CKA-aware pruning保留的structures\n      对GSM8K distribution更specific而非general reasoning structures。\n      所有recovered模型的OOD performance大幅低于dense baseline\n      （MATH-500: 24-30% vs 52%），说明pruning+recovery的reasoning preservation\n      对distribution shift很脆弱。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 13: OOD Evaluation\"\n        columns: [\"Model\", \"GSM8K\", \"MATH-500\", \"HumanEval\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Dense Baseline\", \"76.4%\", \"52%\", \"58%\"]\n          - [\"RASP-20 + GRPO\", \"57.8%\", \"24%\", \"31%\"]\n          - [\"Standard-20 + GRPO\", \"62.1%\", \"28%\", \"35%\"]\n          - [\"Standard-20 + SFT\", \"63.5%\", \"30%\", \"37%\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Radar chart: 4个模型在3个benchmark上的coverage\"\n      - \"Recovery rate by domain: GSM8K vs MATH-500 vs HumanEval的recovery rates对比\"\n    analysis: >\n      OOD results消除了\"Standard SFT recovery只是memorization\"的concern——\n      Standard在所有domains上都consistently better。\n      RASP在OOD上的劣势进一步weaken了recovery-aware pruning的motivation。\n      论文中：recovery后的OOD degradation是under-explored area，\n      无论pruning方法如何，recovery都有significant OOD cost。\n\n  - name: \"Bonsai Baseline 20%\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_013\"\n    description: \"Bonsai（ICML 2025 gradient-free structured pruning）在20%下的baseline\"\n    expected_results:\n      bonsai_20_postprune_gsm8k_100: 0.25\n      bonsai_20_post_sft_100: 0.59\n      bonsai_20_post_grpo_100: 0.58\n      bonsai_vs_standard_postprune_pp: -3\n      bonsai_vs_standard_post_sft_pp: -5\n    result_rationale: >\n      Bonsai作为gradient-free方法在post-prune略低于Standard/RASP（25% vs 27-29%），\n      因为它不使用gradient信号。SFT recovery后达到59%，\n      与RASP（57%）comparable但低于Standard（64%）。\n      GRPO同样无额外增益。\n      Bonsai的表现pattern与RASP/Standard一致——SFT是primary recovery driver，\n      pruning method间差异在recovery后收敛。\n      作为lower-priority baseline，主要价值是扩展method coverage。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 14: Bonsai Baseline\"\n        columns: [\"Stage\", \"Bonsai-20\", \"RASP-20\", \"Standard-20\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Post-Prune\", \"25%\", \"29%\", \"28%\"]\n          - [\"Post-SFT\", \"59%\", \"57%\", \"64%\"]\n          - [\"Post-GRPO\", \"58%\", \"59%\", \"63%\"]\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      Bonsai加入后method coverage达到4种（RASP, Standard, GRASPrune, Bonsai）。\n      Pattern一致：post-prune差异大，SFT recovery后差异缩小，GRPO无额外贡献。\n      strengthen了\"recovery dominates pruning structure\"的narrative。\n\n  - name: \"CKA Reliability Analysis\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_014\"\n    description: \"CKA scoring的split-half consistency和calibration size sensitivity\"\n    expected_results:\n      split_half_spearman_rho: 0.93\n      split_half_p_value: \"<0.0001\"\n      cal_256_vs_512_rank_correlation: 0.96\n      cal_512_vs_1024_rank_correlation: 0.98\n      cal_256_vs_1024_rank_correlation: 0.94\n      cka_score_cv_across_splits: 0.04\n    result_rationale: >\n      CKA scoring本身是highly reliable（ρ=0.93, consistent across calibration sizes）。\n      这是一个important nuance：CKA作为measurement工具是可靠的，\n      问题不在于CKA的reliability而在于它measured property（functional overlap）\n      与recoverability之间的relationship是weak的。\n      Split-half ρ=0.93说明CKA scores不是noisy estimates——\n      它们accurately capture了functional overlap，只是这个overlap不predicts recovery。\n      Cal size sensitivity低（256→1024 rank correlation >0.94）说明256 samples足够。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 15: CKA Reliability\"\n        columns: [\"Metric\", \"Value\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Split-half Spearman ρ\", \"0.93\"]\n          - [\"Cal 256 vs 1024 rank ρ\", \"0.94\"]\n          - [\"CKA score CV across splits\", \"0.04\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Split-half scatter: two halves的CKA scores高度correlated\"\n    analysis: >\n      CKA reliability高strengthens negative finding的credibility——\n      不是因为measurement noise导致CKA不predictive，\n      而是functional overlap genuinely不是recoverability的good predictor。\n      论文中这作为methodological rigor的evidence。\n\n  - name: \"α Sensitivity Ablation\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_015\"\n    description: \"α ∈ {0, 0.25, 0.5, 1, 2, 4} sweep在RASP scoring S(h)=I(h)×(1-F(h))^α\"\n    expected_results:\n      alpha_0_gsm8k_100: 0.28\n      alpha_0p25_gsm8k_100: 0.28\n      alpha_0p5_gsm8k_100: 0.29\n      alpha_1p0_gsm8k_100: 0.30\n      alpha_2p0_gsm8k_100: 0.34\n      alpha_4p0_gsm8k_100: 0.40\n      alpha_optimal: 4.0\n      alpha_0_vs_optimal_gap_pp: 12\n      alpha_monotonic: true\n      alpha_1p0_sft_recovery: 0.59\n      alpha_4p0_sft_recovery: 0.62\n      alpha_0_sft_recovery: 0.64\n    result_rationale: >\n      α=0即Standard pruning（28%），α=4.0给出最优post-prune（40%，+12pp，已观测）。\n      Relationship monotonically increasing with α，suggesting α主要作为importance score的\n      exponential rescaling——higher α更aggressively保护high-importance structures。\n      但关键反转发生在SFT recovery后：α=0（Standard）恢复到64%，\n      α=4.0恢复到62%，α=1.0恢复到59%。\n      Post-prune advantage（α=4.0 > α=0 by 12pp）在SFT recovery后不仅消失还反转\n      （α=0 > α=4.0 by 2pp）。\n      这是worst档最subtle但重要的finding：α scaling优化了wrong objective（post-prune accuracy）\n      而非最终目标（post-recovery accuracy）。\n      RASP的α scaling helps post-prune但hurts recovery——\n      因为它over-protects structures that are important but not SFT-recoverable，\n      同时under-removes structures that are less important but carry SFT-friendly gradients。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 16: α Ablation Results\"\n        columns: [\"α\", \"Post-Prune GSM8K\", \"Post-SFT GSM8K\", \"Post-SFT→GRPO\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"0 (Standard)\", \"28%\", \"64%\", \"63%\"]\n          - [\"0.25\", \"28%\", \"63%\", \"62%\"]\n          - [\"0.5\", \"29%\", \"62%\", \"62%\"]\n          - [\"1.0\", \"30%\", \"59%\", \"60%\"]\n          - [\"2.0\", \"34%\", \"60%\", \"60%\"]\n          - [\"4.0\", \"40%\", \"62%\", \"59%\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Dual-axis plot: α vs post-prune accuracy (ascending) 和 α vs post-recovery accuracy (U-shaped/flat)\"\n      - \"Pareto frontier: post-prune vs post-recovery accuracy across α values\"\n    analysis: >\n      α ablation是worst档最nuanced的finding。\n      Post-prune: α scaling works（monotonic improvement up to +12pp）。\n      Post-recovery: α scaling effect vanishes or reverses。\n      这creates an interesting decoupling：optimizing post-prune ≠ optimizing post-recovery。\n      论文positive takeaway：α scaling确实是effective pruning intervention，\n      但其mechanism是importance distribution reshaping而非CKA-driven recoverability prediction。\n      Post-recovery的non-monotonic pattern suggests α=0（no CKA weighting）\n      可能accidentally produce structures that are more SFT-receptive。\n\n  - name: \"Inference Speedup Benchmark\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_016\"\n    description: \"Dense vs RASP-20 vs Standard-20的wall-clock latency和throughput对比\"\n    expected_results:\n      dense_latency_ms_per_token: 28.5\n      rasp_20_latency_ms_per_token: 25.2\n      standard_20_latency_ms_per_token: 25.0\n      speedup_rasp_vs_dense: 1.13\n      speedup_standard_vs_dense: 1.14\n      dense_throughput_tokens_per_sec: 35.1\n      rasp_20_throughput: 39.7\n      standard_20_throughput: 40.0\n      memory_reduction_percent: 18.5\n      rasp_vs_standard_speedup_diff: \"<1%\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Structured pruning at 20%理论上减少20% FLOPs，\n      但实际speedup仅~1.13x due to hardware underutilization at small batch sizes\n      和memory bandwidth bottlenecks。\n      RASP和Standard的speedup几乎identical（1.13x vs 1.14x）因为两者prune相同数量的structures，\n      只是选择了不同的specific structures。\n      Memory reduction (~18.5%)接近理论值，这是structured pruning的practical advantage。\n      Speedup ratio在[1.08, 1.18]范围内，符合worst档预期——\n      不算impressive但足以demonstrate structured pruning的practical motivation。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 17: Inference Speedup\"\n        columns: [\"Model\", \"Latency (ms/tok)\", \"Throughput (tok/s)\", \"Memory (GB)\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Dense\", \"28.5\", \"35.1\", \"14.2\"]\n          - [\"RASP-20\", \"25.2\", \"39.7\", \"11.6\"]\n          - [\"Standard-20\", \"25.0\", \"40.0\", \"11.5\"]\n          - [\"Speedup vs Dense\", \"1.13×/1.14×\", \"1.13×/1.14×\", \"18.3%/19.0% saved\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Bar chart: latency comparison with error bars\"\n    analysis: >\n      Speedup modest but real (1.13x)。两种pruning方法的efficiency完全相同。\n      这reinforces worst档的point：pruning structure选择不影响practical outcomes\n      （neither accuracy post-recovery nor inference efficiency）。\n      论文中作为实用性baseline data。\n\n  - name: \"Unstructured Pruning Baseline 20%\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_017\"\n    description: \"Magnitude-based unstructured pruning at 20%作为对比baseline\"\n    expected_results:\n      unstructured_20_postprune_gsm8k_100: 0.56\n      unstructured_20_postprune_gsm8k_1319: 0.545\n      unstructured_20_post_sft_100: 0.64\n      unstructured_20_post_grpo_100: 0.65\n      unstructured_20_post_grpo_1319: 0.635\n      unstructured_vs_best_structured_pp: -0.5\n      unstructured_speedup_ratio: 1.02\n      unstructured_memory_saved: 0\n    result_rationale: >\n      Unstructured pruning at 20%保留了远多于structured pruning的post-prune accuracy\n      （56% vs 28-29%）因为它pruning individual weights而非entire channel groups。\n      SFT recovery仅marginal gain（56%→64%），因为post-prune already decent。\n      GRPO adds 1pp to 65%。\n      但unstructured pruning几乎无speedup（1.02x）因为sparse tensors不efficiently map to GPU hardware。\n      最终recovered accuracy（65%）与structured Standard+SFT（64%）comparable——\n      structured pruning通过recovery \"catches up\" to unstructured的保留能力。\n      这是一个interesting finding for worst档：\n      structured pruning + SFT recovery ≈ unstructured pruning in accuracy，\n      但structured provides real speedup（1.13x vs 1.02x）。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 18: Unstructured vs Structured Comparison\"\n        columns: [\"Method\", \"Post-Prune\", \"Post-Recovery\", \"Speedup\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Unstructured 20%\", \"54.5%\", \"63.5%\", \"1.02×\"]\n          - [\"RASP-20 (structured)\", \"29.3%\", \"57.8%\", \"1.13×\"]\n          - [\"Standard-20 (structured)\", \"28.1%\", \"63.5%\", \"1.14×\"]\n          - [\"GRASPrune-20 (structured)\", \"7.2%\", \"55.0%\", \"1.13×\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Accuracy vs speedup scatter: unstructured在upper-left (high acc, low speedup)，structured在lower-right\"\n    analysis: >\n      Unstructured vs structured comparison highlights the recovery gap：\n      structured pruning损伤severe但SFT几乎完全bridges这个gap。\n      Standard structured + SFT matches unstructured accuracy while providing real speedup。\n      这进一步supports SFT recovery的power——\n      它能overcome 27pp的post-prune deficit（unstructured 55% vs structured 28%）\n      到达相同的recovered accuracy。\n\n  - name: \"SFT OOD Eval Contingency\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_018\"\n    description: \"SFT-recovered Standard模型在MATH-500和HumanEval上的OOD评估\"\n    expected_results:\n      sft_standard_20_math500: 0.30\n      sft_standard_20_humaneval: 0.37\n      sft_rasp_20_math500: 0.25\n      sft_rasp_20_humaneval: 0.31\n      dense_math500: 0.52\n      dense_humaneval: 0.58\n      standard_sft_math500_recovery_rate: 0.42\n      rasp_sft_math500_recovery_rate: 0.35\n      standard_vs_rasp_ood_gap_math500_pp: 5\n      standard_vs_rasp_ood_gap_humaneval_pp: 6\n    result_rationale: >\n      Standard的SFT recovery（1%→64% GSM8K jump——虽然在reeval后是28%→64%）\n      是否只是GSM8K pattern memorization？OOD eval显示NO：\n      Standard在MATH-500（30%）和HumanEval（37%）上也consistently outperform RASP（25%, 31%）。\n      Standard的OOD advantage（+5-6pp）甚至略大于in-distribution advantage（+7pp GSM8K），\n      说明Standard的SFT recovery建立了genuinely better reasoning ability而非memorization。\n      这是worst档对RASP最damaging的evidence之一——\n      即使在OOD evaluation下RASP也consistently inferior。\n      Recovery后的OOD performance大幅低于dense baseline\n      （MATH-500: 25-30% vs 52%），indicating significant OOD fragility for all pruned models。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 19: SFT OOD Evaluation\"\n        columns: [\"Model\", \"GSM8K (ID)\", \"MATH-500 (OOD)\", \"HumanEval (OOD)\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Dense\", \"76.4%\", \"52%\", \"58%\"]\n          - [\"Standard-20 + SFT\", \"63.5%\", \"30%\", \"37%\"]\n          - [\"RASP-20 + SFT\", \"55.3%\", \"25%\", \"31%\"]\n          - [\"Δ (Std−RASP)\", \"+8.2pp\", \"+5pp\", \"+6pp\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Grouped bar chart: ID vs OOD performance for SFT-recovered models\"\n    analysis: >\n      OOD eval eliminates memorization concern。Standard的recovery advantage is genuine。\n      论文中这应作为robustness evidence，\n      framed as：Standard pruning + SFT produces more generalizable recovery than RASP + SFT。\n      Implication：CKA-aware structure selection优化了wrong representational properties，\n      可能保留了task-specific circuits而非general reasoning scaffolding。\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":13279,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":13279},"output_tokens":27,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7505ab55-e481-40a0-9dc6-f07ebf7a7c55","uuid":"7561c5d3-2822-4546-8f17-2e960a455b4f"}
{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"api_error_status":null,"duration_ms":286499,"duration_api_ms":287765,"num_turns":1,"result":"```yaml\ntier: worst\nnarrative_guidance: >\n  完全reframe为\"Do Reasoning LLMs Need Recovery-Aware Pruning?\"——controlled empirical study，\n  核心发现是surprising negative result：CKA functional overlap不预测RLVR recoverability，\n  但α-scaled importance scoring确实优于vanilla magnitude pruning（与CKA理论联系薄弱），\n  SFT recovery对所有pruning方法都surprisingly effective。\n  GRPO未能逆转Standard在SFT阶段建立的优势，RASP在GRPO下无额外增益甚至略劣。\n  论文价值在于：(1)实验thoroughness本身（5-seed, 3 sparsity, 4 methods, 2 recovery paradigms），\n  (2)α scoring作为简单有效的pruning改进的positive takeaway，\n  (3)对recovery-aware pruning直觉假设的empirically grounded challenge。\n\nimagined_experiments:\n  - name: \"Full GSM8K Eval N=1319 (Post-Prune)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_001\"\n    description: \"Dense baseline + RASP_20 + Standard_20 在完整1319样本上的post-prune评估\"\n    expected_results:\n      dense_baseline_gsm8k_1319: 0.764\n      dense_baseline_ci95: \"±0.023\"\n      rasp_20_gsm8k_1319: 0.293\n      rasp_20_ci95: \"±0.025\"\n      standard_20_gsm8k_1319: 0.281\n      standard_20_ci95: \"±0.025\"\n      rasp_vs_standard_gap_pp: 1.2\n      gap_p_value_bootstrap: 0.34\n      n_samples: 1319\n    result_rationale: >\n      N=100时观测到31% vs 27%（4pp gap），但bootstrap CI为±9pp。\n      扩展到N=1319后CI缩至±2.5pp，真实gap收缩到~1.2pp，\n      因为N=100的4pp gap本身就在seed方差范围内（reeval_postprune_definitive已显示）。\n      RASP的CKA加权在20% sparsity下只重排了少量边界MLP groups，\n      大部分pruning决策与Standard一致（两者共享~85%的pruned set），\n      导致full eval下gap不显著。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 1: Post-Prune GSM8K Accuracy (N=1319)\"\n        columns: [\"Model\", \"Accuracy\", \"95% CI\", \"vs Dense Drop\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Dense Baseline\", \"76.4%\", \"±2.3pp\", \"—\"]\n          - [\"RASP-20\", \"29.3%\", \"±2.5pp\", \"-47.1pp\"]\n          - [\"Standard-20\", \"28.1%\", \"±2.5pp\", \"-48.3pp\"]\n          - [\"Δ (RASP − Standard)\", \"+1.2pp\", \"\", \"p=0.34\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Bar chart: 三个模型的GSM8K accuracy with error bars，视觉上RASP和Standard几乎无法区分\"\n    analysis: >\n      核心发现：原始29% vs 1%的29x优势不可复现（已在reeval_postprune_definitive确认），\n      full eval进一步确认gap仅~1pp且不显著。\n      这直接摧毁了Claim 1的基础——RASP并未在post-prune阶段提供qualitatively different的保留。\n      两种pruning方法都将模型从76%打到~29%，损失相似。\n      论文中需reframe为：在moderate sparsity下，CKA-aware reranking对post-prune accuracy影响有限。\n\n  - name: \"SFT Warmup Recovery\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_002\"\n    description: \"SFT teacher-forcing恢复RASP_20和Standard_20的基本生成能力\"\n    expected_results:\n      sft_rasp_20_gsm8k_100: 0.57\n      sft_standard_20_gsm8k_100: 0.64\n      sft_gap_pp: -7\n      sft_rasp_train_loss_final: 0.64\n      sft_standard_train_loss_final: 0.64\n      sft_rasp_token_accuracy: 0.83\n      sft_standard_token_accuracy: 0.83\n      eos_rate_both: 0.99\n      total_steps: 1870\n    result_rationale: >\n      已完成实验（DONE）。Standard在SFT后反超RASP 7pp（64% vs 57%）。\n      这在worst档下的解释：RASP保护了functionally unique但SFT-unfriendly的structures，\n      而Standard保留了对teacher-forcing更responsive的structures。\n      两者train loss和token accuracy完全相同（0.64, 83%），\n      说明差异不在optimization landscape而在pruned model的representational capacity分配上。\n      关键是：SFT recovery本身extremely effective——从29%→57%/64%，恢复了大部分能力。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 2: SFT Recovery Results\"\n        columns: [\"Pruned Model\", \"Post-Prune\", \"Post-SFT\", \"Recovery Gain\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"RASP-20\", \"29%\", \"57%\", \"+28pp\"]\n          - [\"Standard-20\", \"28%\", \"64%\", \"+36pp\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Training loss curves: 两条曲线几乎完全重合，最终都收敛到0.64\"\n    analysis: >\n      Standard的SFT recovery优势（+36pp vs +28pp）是worst档的关键evidence：\n      recovery更多取决于training signal（SFT data）而非pruning structure。\n      Standard保留的structures虽然CKA overlap更高，但对SFT的gradient信号更receptive。\n\n  - name: \"GRPO Stage-2 Recovery\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_003\"\n    description: \"在SFT-warmed模型上运行GRPO reinforcement learning恢复\"\n    expected_results:\n      grpo_rasp_20_gsm8k_100: 0.59\n      grpo_standard_20_gsm8k_100: 0.63\n      grpo_rasp_vs_sft_gain_pp: 2\n      grpo_standard_vs_sft_gain_pp: -1\n      grpo_gap_pp: -4\n      grpo_rasp_reward_mean_final: 0.42\n      grpo_standard_reward_mean_final: 0.45\n      training_stable: true\n      convergence_step: 800\n    result_rationale: >\n      已完成（DONE, conclusion: negative）。GRPO未能逆转SFT阶段Standard的优势。\n      RASP从57%→59%（+2pp marginal gain），Standard从64%→63%（-1pp，轻微regression）。\n      GRPO在两个模型上的增益都很小，说明SFT已经capture了大部分recoverable performance，\n      GRPO的RL信号在moderate sparsity下缺乏足够的capacity来进一步优化。\n      这与\"GRPO对pruned模型的恢复效果不稳定\"的核心假设一致。\n      Standard的轻微regression可能是GRPO的exploration noise覆盖了SFT学到的patterns。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 3: GRPO Recovery Results\"\n        columns: [\"Model\", \"Post-SFT\", \"Post-GRPO\", \"GRPO Gain\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"RASP-20\", \"57%\", \"59%\", \"+2pp\"]\n          - [\"Standard-20\", \"64%\", \"63%\", \"-1pp\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"GRPO reward curves: 两条曲线都plateau早（~step 800），RASP略低于Standard\"\n      - \"GSM8K accuracy over GRPO steps: 几乎flat，偶尔spike但不稳定\"\n    analysis: >\n      GRPO作为recovery method的added value可疑——SFT alone已达到comparable或更好的结果。\n      这是worst档的decisive evidence：sft_vs_grpo_interaction_significant = False。\n      无论pruning方法如何，GRPO都不提供超过SFT的显著恢复。\n      论文需要reframe：recovery robustness来自training signal（SFT data quality），\n      而非pruning-recovery的structural alignment。\n\n  - name: \"Full GSM8K Eval N=1319 (All Recovered Models)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_004\"\n    description: \"所有recovered模型在完整1319样本上的最终评估\"\n    expected_results:\n      dense_baseline_1319: 0.764\n      sft_rasp_20_1319: 0.553\n      sft_standard_20_1319: 0.635\n      grpo_rasp_20_1319: 0.578\n      grpo_standard_20_1319: 0.621\n      sft_rasp_ci95: \"±0.027\"\n      sft_standard_ci95: \"±0.026\"\n      grpo_rasp_ci95: \"±0.027\"\n      grpo_standard_ci95: \"±0.026\"\n      grpo_vs_sft_rasp_diff: 2.5\n      grpo_vs_sft_standard_diff: -1.4\n      best_overall: \"SFT-Standard (63.5%)\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      N=1319会轻微调整N=100的点估计（regression to mean效应）。\n      SFT Standard的64%可能微降至63.5%，SFT RASP的57%降至55.3%。\n      GRPO模型的full eval同样显示Standard优势持续。\n      关键发现：best recovered model是SFT-only Standard（63.5%），不需要GRPO也不需要RASP。\n      这是worst档最damaging的result——最简单的pipeline（Standard pruning + SFT）给出最好结果。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 4: Full Pipeline Comparison (N=1319)\"\n        columns: [\"Pipeline\", \"Post-Prune\", \"Post-Recovery\", \"Recovery Rate\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"RASP + SFT\", \"29.3%\", \"55.3%\", \"55.4%\"]\n          - [\"RASP + SFT→GRPO\", \"29.3%\", \"57.8%\", \"60.7%\"]\n          - [\"Standard + SFT\", \"28.1%\", \"63.5%\", \"73.0%\"]\n          - [\"Standard + SFT→GRPO\", \"28.1%\", \"62.1%\", \"70.1%\"]\n          - [\"Dense (no pruning)\", \"—\", \"76.4%\", \"—\"]\n        note: \"Recovery Rate = (post_recovery - post_prune) / (dense - post_prune)\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Grouped bar chart: 4 pipelines的post-prune → post-SFT → post-GRPO三阶段accuracy\"\n      - \"Recovery rate scatter: x=post-prune, y=recovery rate, 标注每个pipeline\"\n    analysis: >\n      Paper Table 1的核心数据。Worst档的narrative：Standard+SFT是Pareto optimal——\n      比所有其他pipeline更简单且更好。RASP的CKA-aware pruning反而hurt了SFT recovery。\n      GRPO在两种pruning上的marginal/negative contribution质疑了RLVR recovery的必要性\n      （至少在moderate sparsity下）。\n\n  - name: \"GRASPrune Baseline 20%\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_005\"\n    description: \"GRASPrune（ACL 2026 SOTA）在20% sparsity下的完整pipeline：prune→eval→SFT→GRPO\"\n    expected_results:\n      grasp_20_postprune_gsm8k_100: 0.08\n      grasp_20_postprune_gsm8k_1319: 0.072\n      grasp_20_eos_rate: 0.02\n      grasp_20_post_sft_gsm8k_100: 0.58\n      grasp_20_post_sft_gsm8k_1319: 0.56\n      grasp_20_post_grpo_gsm8k_100: 0.57\n      grasp_20_post_grpo_gsm8k_1319: 0.55\n      grasp_sft_recovery_gain_pp: 50\n      grasp_grpo_additional_gain_pp: -1\n    result_rationale: >\n      GRASPrune的post-prune accuracy极低（8%，已从grasp_baseline_westd观测到），\n      因为它优化的是budgeted pruning的immediate loss而非reasoning preservation。\n      但SFT recovery将其从8%拉到~58%（+50pp），这是worst档最重要的evidence之一：\n      post-prune accuracy与recovery outcome的correlation远低于预期。\n      GRASPrune post-prune最差（8%）但recovery后与RASP（57.8%）comparable。\n      这直接反驳了\"RASP preserves recoverable structures\"的claim——\n      即使post-prune被摧毁到8%，SFT也能恢复到相似水平。\n      GRPO对GRASPrune同样无额外增益（-1pp regression）。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 5: GRASPrune Pipeline Results\"\n        columns: [\"Stage\", \"Accuracy\", \"Gain from Previous\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Post-Prune\", \"7.2%\", \"-69.2pp from dense\"]\n          - [\"Post-SFT\", \"56.0%\", \"+48.8pp\"]\n          - [\"Post-SFT→GRPO\", \"55.0%\", \"-1.0pp\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Recovery trajectory plot: GRASPrune vs RASP vs Standard的三阶段accuracy变化，GRASPrune呈V形恢复\"\n    analysis: >\n      GRASPrune的V形恢复是worst档的smoking gun：post-prune accuracy几乎不预测recovery outcome。\n      8%→56%的恢复意味着SFT的training signal足以重建大部分reasoning ability，\n      regardless of which structures were pruned。\n      这对所有recovery-aware pruning方法（包括RASP）都是existential challenge：\n      如果recovery主要由training data驱动，优化pruning structure的marginal value极小。\n\n  - name: \"Multi-Seed Post-Prune Eval (5 Seeds)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_006\"\n    description: \"5个random seeds下RASP_20和Standard_20的post-prune GSM8K评估\"\n    expected_results:\n      rasp_20_seed42: 0.293\n      rasp_20_seed123: 0.285\n      rasp_20_seed456: 0.301\n      rasp_20_seed789: 0.278\n      rasp_20_seed1024: 0.289\n      rasp_20_mean: 0.289\n      rasp_20_std: 0.008\n      standard_20_seed42: 0.281\n      standard_20_seed123: 0.275\n      standard_20_seed456: 0.292\n      standard_20_seed789: 0.269\n      standard_20_seed1024: 0.283\n      standard_20_mean: 0.280\n      standard_20_std: 0.008\n      pairwise_gap_mean_pp: 0.9\n      pairwise_gap_std: 0.6\n      paired_t_test_p: 0.15\n      wilcoxon_p: 0.19\n      cohens_d: 0.35\n    result_rationale: >\n      5-seed评估下，RASP和Standard的均值gap约0.9pp，标准差~0.8pp。\n      Paired t-test p=0.15，Wilcoxon p=0.19——均不达显著性阈值（p<0.05）。\n      Cohen's d=0.35属于small effect size。\n      seed-to-seed的方差（~0.8pp std）与gap本身（0.9pp）同量级，\n      说明观测到的gap完全可以被eval noise解释。\n      Worst档的关键：5-seed的power不足以detect <1pp的真实差异，\n      但这恰恰说明即使存在真实差异也太小to be practically meaningful。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 6: Multi-Seed Post-Prune Results\"\n        columns: [\"Seed\", \"RASP-20\", \"Standard-20\", \"Δ\"]\n        rows:\n          - [42, \"29.3%\", \"28.1%\", \"+1.2pp\"]\n          - [123, \"28.5%\", \"27.5%\", \"+1.0pp\"]\n          - [456, \"30.1%\", \"29.2%\", \"+0.9pp\"]\n          - [789, \"27.8%\", \"26.9%\", \"+0.9pp\"]\n          - [1024, \"28.9%\", \"28.3%\", \"+0.6pp\"]\n          - [\"Mean±Std\", \"28.9±0.8%\", \"28.0±0.8%\", \"+0.9±0.6pp\"]\n          - [\"p-value\", \"\", \"\", \"0.15 (paired-t)\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Paired dot plot: 每个seed一条线连接RASP和Standard，几乎所有线都近乎水平\"\n      - \"Box plot: RASP和Standard的5-seed分布高度重叠\"\n    analysis: >\n      Post-prune gap在统计上不显著（p=0.15），effect size小（d=0.35）。\n      论文中应honest report这个null result，\n      并argue这个negative finding本身有价值：\n      在moderate sparsity下CKA reranking不改变pruning outcome。\n\n  - name: \"Scoring Ablation at 20% Sparsity\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_007\"\n    description: \"magnitude-only, gradient-only, random pruning对比RASP/Standard\"\n    expected_results:\n      magnitude_only_gsm8k_100: 0.27\n      gradient_only_gsm8k_100: 0.26\n      random_pruning_gsm8k_100: 0.14\n      rasp_alpha4_gsm8k_100: 0.40\n      standard_alpha0_gsm8k_100: 0.28\n      rasp_alpha1_gsm8k_100: 0.30\n      magnitude_only_gsm8k_1319: 0.265\n      gradient_only_gsm8k_1319: 0.255\n      random_pruning_gsm8k_1319: 0.135\n    result_rationale: >\n      Random pruning大幅劣于所有structured方法（14% vs 26-40%），证明pruning order matters。\n      Magnitude-only（27%）≈ Standard（28%）≈ Gradient-only（26%），\n      三种importance-based方法在moderate sparsity下几乎等价。\n      RASP α=4（40%）显著优于所有α=0方法——但这主要是α scaling的效果，不是CKA。\n      关键ablation：α=1（CKA权重较弱）只给30%，仅比Standard好2pp。\n      α=4的大幅提升（+12pp over Standard）更可能是importance distribution的reshaping效应\n      （α放大了high-overlap groups的penalty，但也放大了importance的tail），\n      而非CKA functional overlap的predictive value。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 7: Scoring Ablation (N=100, 20% Sparsity)\"\n        columns: [\"Scoring Method\", \"Post-Prune GSM8K\", \"vs Standard Δ\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Random\", \"14%\", \"-14pp\"]\n          - [\"Gradient-only\", \"26%\", \"-2pp\"]\n          - [\"Magnitude-only\", \"27%\", \"-1pp\"]\n          - [\"Standard (Wanda I(h))\", \"28%\", \"—\"]\n          - [\"RASP α=1.0\", \"30%\", \"+2pp\"]\n          - [\"RASP α=4.0\", \"40%\", \"+12pp\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Bar chart: 6种scoring方法的post-prune accuracy，α=4.0是clear outlier\"\n      - \"Decomposition plot: 将α=4.0的12pp gain分解为importance-scaling vs CKA-specific贡献\"\n    analysis: >\n      α=4.0的优势（+12pp）是worst档的positive takeaway，但解释需要carefully nuanced。\n      α scaling本质上改变了importance score的distribution shape——\n      它upweight了already-important structures并downweight了marginal ones，\n      CKA项(1-F(h))只是这个rescaling的vehicle之一。\n      为证明这一点：可以test α-scaled magnitude-only（I(h)^α without CKA），\n      如果效果similar则CKA的独立贡献为零。\n      论文中应将此framed为\"α-scaled importance scoring improves pruning\"而非\"CKA predicts recoverability\"。\n\n  - name: \"CKA-Recoverability Correlation Analysis\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_008\"\n    description: \"Per-structure CKA F(h)与post-recovery accuracy retention的mixed-effects regression\"\n    expected_results:\n      n_mlp_groups: 784\n      n_pruned_mlp_groups: 200\n      cka_beta_coefficient: 0.08\n      cka_beta_p_value: 0.12\n      cka_incremental_r2: 0.018\n      weight_norm_beta: 0.23\n      weight_norm_p: 0.001\n      gradient_importance_beta: 0.31\n      gradient_importance_p: 0.0003\n      activation_magnitude_beta: 0.19\n      activation_magnitude_p: 0.004\n      full_model_r2: 0.34\n      model_without_cka_r2: 0.32\n      layer_random_effect_variance: 0.15\n      cka_spearman_with_recoverability: 0.11\n      cka_spearman_p: 0.09\n    result_rationale: >\n      Mixed-effects regression显示CKA β=0.08 (p=0.12)，不达显著性。\n      Incremental R²仅0.018（1.8%），远低于useful predictor的阈值（通常>5%）。\n      相比之下weight norm（β=0.23, p=0.001）和gradient importance（β=0.31, p=0.0003）\n      都是stronger predictors。\n      CKA functional overlap与recoverability的Spearman ρ=0.11（p=0.09），borderline但不显著。\n      核心问题：CKA measures inter-head functional similarity，\n      但RLVR recovery不是通过\"redistribute function across heads\"实现的——\n      RLVR更多是global optimization of the loss landscape，\n      individual head的functional overlap对global recovery的predictive power有限。\n      Layer random effect variance (0.15)较大，说明per-layer差异比per-head CKA更重要。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 8: Mixed-Effects Regression Results (MLP Groups, N=784)\"\n        columns: [\"Predictor\", \"β\", \"SE\", \"p-value\", \"Incremental R²\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Gradient Importance\", \"0.31\", \"0.06\", \"<0.001\", \"0.14\"]\n          - [\"Weight Norm\", \"0.23\", \"0.05\", \"0.001\", \"0.09\"]\n          - [\"Activation Magnitude\", \"0.19\", \"0.05\", \"0.004\", \"0.06\"]\n          - [\"CKA Overlap F(h)\", \"0.08\", \"0.05\", \"0.12\", \"0.018\"]\n          - [\"Full Model R²\", \"\", \"\", \"\", \"0.34\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Scatter plot: F(h) vs per-head recoverability，大量scatter，弱correlation线\"\n      - \"Coefficient plot: 4个predictor的β with 95% CI，CKA的CI跨零\"\n      - \"Partial regression plot: 控制其他变量后CKA的residual effect\"\n    analysis: >\n      这是Claim 2的直接否定。CKA functional overlap不是recoverability的significant predictor。\n      Traditional importance metrics（gradient, weight norm）解释了大部分variance。\n      论文reframe：functional overlap是一个intuitively appealing but empirically unsupported\n      predictor of recovery outcomes。\n      Positive spin：实验thoroughness（N=784, mixed-effects, covariates控制）使这个negative\n      result credible且publishable。\n\n  - name: \"SFT-Only Recovery Comparison\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_009\"\n    description: \"Same pruned models, same data budget, SFT-only recovery（无GRPO）\"\n    expected_results:\n      sft_only_rasp_20_gsm8k_100: 0.57\n      sft_only_rasp_20_gsm8k_1319: 0.553\n      sft_only_standard_20_gsm8k_100: 0.64\n      sft_only_standard_20_gsm8k_1319: 0.635\n      sft_only_gap_pp: -7\n      grpo_rasp_20_gsm8k_1319: 0.578\n      grpo_standard_20_gsm8k_1319: 0.621\n      interaction_f_test_p: 0.41\n      pruning_method_main_effect_p: 0.03\n      recovery_method_main_effect_p: 0.62\n      interaction_effect_size: 0.02\n    result_rationale: >\n      plan_002已完成SFT-only recovery（RASP 57%, Standard 64%）。\n      2×2 ANOVA (pruning × recovery)显示：\n      pruning method有main effect（Standard > RASP, p=0.03），\n      recovery method无main effect（SFT ≈ SFT→GRPO, p=0.62），\n      交互作用不显著（p=0.41）。\n      这意味着：Standard在两种recovery下都优于RASP，\n      且recovery method的选择不改变pruning方法的相对排名。\n      Claim 3（recovery method conditions optimal pruning order）被直接否定。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 9: 2×2 Recovery Comparison (N=1319)\"\n        columns: [\"\", \"SFT-Only\", \"SFT→GRPO\", \"Δ(GRPO−SFT)\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"RASP-20\", \"55.3%\", \"57.8%\", \"+2.5pp\"]\n          - [\"Standard-20\", \"63.5%\", \"62.1%\", \"-1.4pp\"]\n          - [\"Δ(Std−RASP)\", \"+8.2pp\", \"+4.3pp\", \"\"]\n      - name: \"Table 10: 2×2 ANOVA Results\"\n        columns: [\"Effect\", \"F\", \"p-value\", \"η²\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Pruning Method\", \"5.12\", \"0.03\", \"0.08\"]\n          - [\"Recovery Method\", \"0.24\", \"0.62\", \"0.004\"]\n          - [\"Interaction\", \"0.68\", \"0.41\", \"0.02\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Interaction plot: pruning method × recovery method，两条线近乎平行（无交互）\"\n    analysis: >\n      Standard在两种recovery下一致优于RASP，GRPO不改变这个ranking。\n      Interaction plot的平行线直接visualize了null interaction。\n      论文reframe为positive finding：SFT recovery is surprisingly robust——\n      无论pruning structure如何，SFT都能恢复到similar relative levels。\n      这暗示recovery robustness更多来自training signal而非pruning structure。\n\n  - name: \"25% Sparsity RASP + Standard\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_010\"\n    description: \"25% sparsity下完整pipeline：prune→eval→SFT→GRPO\"\n    expected_results:\n      rasp_25_postprune_gsm8k_100: 0.18\n      rasp_25_postprune_gsm8k_1319: 0.172\n      standard_25_postprune_gsm8k_100: 0.16\n      standard_25_postprune_gsm8k_1319: 0.155\n      postprune_gap_25_pp: 1.7\n      rasp_25_post_sft_100: 0.48\n      standard_25_post_sft_100: 0.52\n      rasp_25_post_grpo_100: 0.49\n      standard_25_post_grpo_100: 0.53\n      rasp_25_post_grpo_1319: 0.475\n      standard_25_post_grpo_1319: 0.515\n      recovery_rate_rasp_25: 0.512\n      recovery_rate_standard_25: 0.590\n    result_rationale: >\n      25% sparsity下两种方法都受到更大损伤（17-18% post-prune vs 28-29% at 20%）。\n      RASP仍然略优于Standard在post-prune（+1.7pp），但gap依然不显著。\n      SFT recovery将两者提升到48-52%，Standard再次优于RASP。\n      GRPO在25% sparsity下同样无额外增益（+1pp for RASP, +1pp for Standard）。\n      关键观察：从20%到25%，recovery ceiling从~63%降到~53%（-10pp），\n      说明sparsity对recovery outcome的影响远大于pruning method的影响。\n      这进一步support了worst档的narrative：pruning structure的精细选择\n      相比sparsity ratio本身是second-order effect。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 11: 25% Sparsity Pipeline\"\n        columns: [\"Model\", \"Post-Prune\", \"Post-SFT\", \"Post-GRPO\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"RASP-25\", \"17.2%\", \"48%\", \"49%\"]\n          - [\"Standard-25\", \"15.5%\", \"52%\", \"53%\"]\n          - [\"Δ (RASP−Std)\", \"+1.7pp\", \"-4pp\", \"-4pp\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Sparsity × accuracy curve: 20% and 25%下RASP和Standard的recovery trajectories\"\n      - \"Recovery ceiling plot: sparsity ratio vs best-recovered accuracy\"\n    analysis: >\n      25% sparsity数据确认20%的pattern scales：Standard consistently recovers better，\n      GRPO consistently unhelpful。Sparsity ratio是dominant factor。\n      论文中这作为robustness check，strengthen negative findings的generality。\n\n  - name: \"30% Sparsity Probe\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_011\"\n    description: \"30% sparsity下prune + eval only（无recovery），mapping collapse threshold\"\n    expected_results:\n      rasp_30_postprune_gsm8k_100: 0.05\n      standard_30_postprune_gsm8k_100: 0.04\n      rasp_30_eos_rate: 0.15\n      standard_30_eos_rate: 0.08\n      rasp_30_avg_len: 3200\n      standard_30_avg_len: 3800\n      gap_pp: 1\n    result_rationale: >\n      30% sparsity下两种方法都near-collapse（5% vs 4%），\n      consistent with已知的35% sparsity完全collapse（D005）。\n      RASP的marginal advantage缩小到1pp（在noise范围内）。\n      EOS rate大幅下降说明模型生成能力严重受损。\n      不做recovery是正确决策——从5%恢复的cost-benefit不合理。\n      这个data point完成了sparsity response curve：20%(29%)→25%(17%)→30%(5%)→35%(~0%)。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 12: 30% Sparsity Probe\"\n        columns: [\"Model\", \"Post-Prune\", \"EOS Rate\", \"Avg Length\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"RASP-30\", \"5%\", \"15%\", \"3200\"]\n          - [\"Standard-30\", \"4%\", \"8%\", \"3800\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Sparsity response curve: 0-35% sparsity下的post-prune accuracy for RASP和Standard\"\n    analysis: >\n      30% sparsity是\"no man's land\"——pruning too aggressive for meaningful recovery。\n      两种方法无差异。curve shape（smooth degradation 20-25%, cliff 25-30%）\n      suggests a phase transition around 27-28% sparsity for this model。\n\n  - name: \"OOD Evaluation (MATH-500, HumanEval)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_012\"\n    description: \"Best recovered models在MATH-500和HumanEval上的OOD泛化评估\"\n    expected_results:\n      dense_math500: 0.52\n      dense_humaneval: 0.58\n      grpo_rasp_20_math500: 0.24\n      grpo_rasp_20_humaneval: 0.31\n      grpo_standard_20_math500: 0.28\n      grpo_standard_20_humaneval: 0.35\n      sft_standard_20_math500: 0.30\n      sft_standard_20_humaneval: 0.37\n      rasp_math500_advantage_pp: -4\n      rasp_humaneval_advantage_pp: -4\n      math500_recovery_rate_rasp: 0.36\n      math500_recovery_rate_standard: 0.46\n    result_rationale: >\n      OOD eval显示RASP在MATH-500和HumanEval上均劣于Standard（-4pp each）。\n      Standard的OOD优势与GSM8K上的优势consistent——\n      不是GSM8K-specific pattern memorization而是genuine reasoning recovery。\n      RASP的OOD劣势可能因为CKA-aware pruning保留的structures\n      对GSM8K distribution更specific而非general reasoning structures。\n      所有recovered模型的OOD performance大幅低于dense baseline\n      （MATH-500: 24-30% vs 52%），说明pruning+recovery的reasoning preservation\n      对distribution shift很脆弱。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 13: OOD Evaluation\"\n        columns: [\"Model\", \"GSM8K\", \"MATH-500\", \"HumanEval\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Dense Baseline\", \"76.4%\", \"52%\", \"58%\"]\n          - [\"RASP-20 + GRPO\", \"57.8%\", \"24%\", \"31%\"]\n          - [\"Standard-20 + GRPO\", \"62.1%\", \"28%\", \"35%\"]\n          - [\"Standard-20 + SFT\", \"63.5%\", \"30%\", \"37%\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Radar chart: 4个模型在3个benchmark上的coverage\"\n      - \"Recovery rate by domain: GSM8K vs MATH-500 vs HumanEval的recovery rates对比\"\n    analysis: >\n      OOD results消除了\"Standard SFT recovery只是memorization\"的concern——\n      Standard在所有domains上都consistently better。\n      RASP在OOD上的劣势进一步weaken了recovery-aware pruning的motivation。\n      论文中：recovery后的OOD degradation是under-explored area，\n      无论pruning方法如何，recovery都有significant OOD cost。\n\n  - name: \"Bonsai Baseline 20%\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_013\"\n    description: \"Bonsai（ICML 2025 gradient-free structured pruning）在20%下的baseline\"\n    expected_results:\n      bonsai_20_postprune_gsm8k_100: 0.25\n      bonsai_20_post_sft_100: 0.59\n      bonsai_20_post_grpo_100: 0.58\n      bonsai_vs_standard_postprune_pp: -3\n      bonsai_vs_standard_post_sft_pp: -5\n    result_rationale: >\n      Bonsai作为gradient-free方法在post-prune略低于Standard/RASP（25% vs 27-29%），\n      因为它不使用gradient信号。SFT recovery后达到59%，\n      与RASP（57%）comparable但低于Standard（64%）。\n      GRPO同样无额外增益。\n      Bonsai的表现pattern与RASP/Standard一致——SFT是primary recovery driver，\n      pruning method间差异在recovery后收敛。\n      作为lower-priority baseline，主要价值是扩展method coverage。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 14: Bonsai Baseline\"\n        columns: [\"Stage\", \"Bonsai-20\", \"RASP-20\", \"Standard-20\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Post-Prune\", \"25%\", \"29%\", \"28%\"]\n          - [\"Post-SFT\", \"59%\", \"57%\", \"64%\"]\n          - [\"Post-GRPO\", \"58%\", \"59%\", \"63%\"]\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      Bonsai加入后method coverage达到4种（RASP, Standard, GRASPrune, Bonsai）。\n      Pattern一致：post-prune差异大，SFT recovery后差异缩小，GRPO无额外贡献。\n      strengthen了\"recovery dominates pruning structure\"的narrative。\n\n  - name: \"CKA Reliability Analysis\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_014\"\n    description: \"CKA scoring的split-half consistency和calibration size sensitivity\"\n    expected_results:\n      split_half_spearman_rho: 0.93\n      split_half_p_value: \"<0.0001\"\n      cal_256_vs_512_rank_correlation: 0.96\n      cal_512_vs_1024_rank_correlation: 0.98\n      cal_256_vs_1024_rank_correlation: 0.94\n      cka_score_cv_across_splits: 0.04\n    result_rationale: >\n      CKA scoring本身是highly reliable（ρ=0.93, consistent across calibration sizes）。\n      这是一个important nuance：CKA作为measurement工具是可靠的，\n      问题不在于CKA的reliability而在于它measured property（functional overlap）\n      与recoverability之间的relationship是weak的。\n      Split-half ρ=0.93说明CKA scores不是noisy estimates——\n      它们accurately capture了functional overlap，只是这个overlap不predicts recovery。\n      Cal size sensitivity低（256→1024 rank correlation >0.94）说明256 samples足够。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 15: CKA Reliability\"\n        columns: [\"Metric\", \"Value\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Split-half Spearman ρ\", \"0.93\"]\n          - [\"Cal 256 vs 1024 rank ρ\", \"0.94\"]\n          - [\"CKA score CV across splits\", \"0.04\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Split-half scatter: two halves的CKA scores高度correlated\"\n    analysis: >\n      CKA reliability高strengthens negative finding的credibility——\n      不是因为measurement noise导致CKA不predictive，\n      而是functional overlap genuinely不是recoverability的good predictor。\n      论文中这作为methodological rigor的evidence。\n\n  - name: \"α Sensitivity Ablation\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_015\"\n    description: \"α ∈ {0, 0.25, 0.5, 1, 2, 4} sweep在RASP scoring S(h)=I(h)×(1-F(h))^α\"\n    expected_results:\n      alpha_0_gsm8k_100: 0.28\n      alpha_0p25_gsm8k_100: 0.28\n      alpha_0p5_gsm8k_100: 0.29\n      alpha_1p0_gsm8k_100: 0.30\n      alpha_2p0_gsm8k_100: 0.34\n      alpha_4p0_gsm8k_100: 0.40\n      alpha_optimal: 4.0\n      alpha_0_vs_optimal_gap_pp: 12\n      alpha_monotonic: true\n      alpha_1p0_sft_recovery: 0.59\n      alpha_4p0_sft_recovery: 0.62\n      alpha_0_sft_recovery: 0.64\n    result_rationale: >\n      α=0即Standard pruning（28%），α=4.0给出最优post-prune（40%，+12pp，已观测）。\n      Relationship monotonically increasing with α，suggesting α主要作为importance score的\n      exponential rescaling——higher α更aggressively保护high-importance structures。\n      但关键反转发生在SFT recovery后：α=0（Standard）恢复到64%，\n      α=4.0恢复到62%，α=1.0恢复到59%。\n      Post-prune advantage（α=4.0 > α=0 by 12pp）在SFT recovery后不仅消失还反转\n      （α=0 > α=4.0 by 2pp）。\n      这是worst档最subtle但重要的finding：α scaling优化了wrong objective（post-prune accuracy）\n      而非最终目标（post-recovery accuracy）。\n      RASP的α scaling helps post-prune但hurts recovery——\n      因为它over-protects structures that are important but not SFT-recoverable，\n      同时under-removes structures that are less important but carry SFT-friendly gradients。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 16: α Ablation Results\"\n        columns: [\"α\", \"Post-Prune GSM8K\", \"Post-SFT GSM8K\", \"Post-SFT→GRPO\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"0 (Standard)\", \"28%\", \"64%\", \"63%\"]\n          - [\"0.25\", \"28%\", \"63%\", \"62%\"]\n          - [\"0.5\", \"29%\", \"62%\", \"62%\"]\n          - [\"1.0\", \"30%\", \"59%\", \"60%\"]\n          - [\"2.0\", \"34%\", \"60%\", \"60%\"]\n          - [\"4.0\", \"40%\", \"62%\", \"59%\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Dual-axis plot: α vs post-prune accuracy (ascending) 和 α vs post-recovery accuracy (U-shaped/flat)\"\n      - \"Pareto frontier: post-prune vs post-recovery accuracy across α values\"\n    analysis: >\n      α ablation是worst档最nuanced的finding。\n      Post-prune: α scaling works（monotonic improvement up to +12pp）。\n      Post-recovery: α scaling effect vanishes or reverses。\n      这creates an interesting decoupling：optimizing post-prune ≠ optimizing post-recovery。\n      论文positive takeaway：α scaling确实是effective pruning intervention，\n      但其mechanism是importance distribution reshaping而非CKA-driven recoverability prediction。\n      Post-recovery的non-monotonic pattern suggests α=0（no CKA weighting）\n      可能accidentally produce structures that are more SFT-receptive。\n\n  - name: \"Inference Speedup Benchmark\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_016\"\n    description: \"Dense vs RASP-20 vs Standard-20的wall-clock latency和throughput对比\"\n    expected_results:\n      dense_latency_ms_per_token: 28.5\n      rasp_20_latency_ms_per_token: 25.2\n      standard_20_latency_ms_per_token: 25.0\n      speedup_rasp_vs_dense: 1.13\n      speedup_standard_vs_dense: 1.14\n      dense_throughput_tokens_per_sec: 35.1\n      rasp_20_throughput: 39.7\n      standard_20_throughput: 40.0\n      memory_reduction_percent: 18.5\n      rasp_vs_standard_speedup_diff: \"<1%\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Structured pruning at 20%理论上减少20% FLOPs，\n      但实际speedup仅~1.13x due to hardware underutilization at small batch sizes\n      和memory bandwidth bottlenecks。\n      RASP和Standard的speedup几乎identical（1.13x vs 1.14x）因为两者prune相同数量的structures，\n      只是选择了不同的specific structures。\n      Memory reduction (~18.5%)接近理论值，这是structured pruning的practical advantage。\n      Speedup ratio在[1.08, 1.18]范围内，符合worst档预期——\n      不算impressive但足以demonstrate structured pruning的practical motivation。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 17: Inference Speedup\"\n        columns: [\"Model\", \"Latency (ms/tok)\", \"Throughput (tok/s)\", \"Memory (GB)\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Dense\", \"28.5\", \"35.1\", \"14.2\"]\n          - [\"RASP-20\", \"25.2\", \"39.7\", \"11.6\"]\n          - [\"Standard-20\", \"25.0\", \"40.0\", \"11.5\"]\n          - [\"Speedup vs Dense\", \"1.13×/1.14×\", \"1.13×/1.14×\", \"18.3%/19.0% saved\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Bar chart: latency comparison with error bars\"\n    analysis: >\n      Speedup modest but real (1.13x)。两种pruning方法的efficiency完全相同。\n      这reinforces worst档的point：pruning structure选择不影响practical outcomes\n      （neither accuracy post-recovery nor inference efficiency）。\n      论文中作为实用性baseline data。\n\n  - name: \"Unstructured Pruning Baseline 20%\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_017\"\n    description: \"Magnitude-based unstructured pruning at 20%作为对比baseline\"\n    expected_results:\n      unstructured_20_postprune_gsm8k_100: 0.56\n      unstructured_20_postprune_gsm8k_1319: 0.545\n      unstructured_20_post_sft_100: 0.64\n      unstructured_20_post_grpo_100: 0.65\n      unstructured_20_post_grpo_1319: 0.635\n      unstructured_vs_best_structured_pp: -0.5\n      unstructured_speedup_ratio: 1.02\n      unstructured_memory_saved: 0\n    result_rationale: >\n      Unstructured pruning at 20%保留了远多于structured pruning的post-prune accuracy\n      （56% vs 28-29%）因为它pruning individual weights而非entire channel groups。\n      SFT recovery仅marginal gain（56%→64%），因为post-prune already decent。\n      GRPO adds 1pp to 65%。\n      但unstructured pruning几乎无speedup（1.02x）因为sparse tensors不efficiently map to GPU hardware。\n      最终recovered accuracy（65%）与structured Standard+SFT（64%）comparable——\n      structured pruning通过recovery \"catches up\" to unstructured的保留能力。\n      这是一个interesting finding for worst档：\n      structured pruning + SFT recovery ≈ unstructured pruning in accuracy，\n      但structured provides real speedup（1.13x vs 1.02x）。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 18: Unstructured vs Structured Comparison\"\n        columns: [\"Method\", \"Post-Prune\", \"Post-Recovery\", \"Speedup\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Unstructured 20%\", \"54.5%\", \"63.5%\", \"1.02×\"]\n          - [\"RASP-20 (structured)\", \"29.3%\", \"57.8%\", \"1.13×\"]\n          - [\"Standard-20 (structured)\", \"28.1%\", \"63.5%\", \"1.14×\"]\n          - [\"GRASPrune-20 (structured)\", \"7.2%\", \"55.0%\", \"1.13×\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Accuracy vs speedup scatter: unstructured在upper-left (high acc, low speedup)，structured在lower-right\"\n    analysis: >\n      Unstructured vs structured comparison highlights the recovery gap：\n      structured pruning损伤severe但SFT几乎完全bridges这个gap。\n      Standard structured + SFT matches unstructured accuracy while providing real speedup。\n      这进一步supports SFT recovery的power——\n      它能overcome 27pp的post-prune deficit（unstructured 55% vs structured 28%）\n      到达相同的recovered accuracy。\n\n  - name: \"SFT OOD Eval Contingency\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_018\"\n    description: \"SFT-recovered Standard模型在MATH-500和HumanEval上的OOD评估\"\n    expected_results:\n      sft_standard_20_math500: 0.30\n      sft_standard_20_humaneval: 0.37\n      sft_rasp_20_math500: 0.25\n      sft_rasp_20_humaneval: 0.31\n      dense_math500: 0.52\n      dense_humaneval: 0.58\n      standard_sft_math500_recovery_rate: 0.42\n      rasp_sft_math500_recovery_rate: 0.35\n      standard_vs_rasp_ood_gap_math500_pp: 5\n      standard_vs_rasp_ood_gap_humaneval_pp: 6\n    result_rationale: >\n      Standard的SFT recovery（1%→64% GSM8K jump——虽然在reeval后是28%→64%）\n      是否只是GSM8K pattern memorization？OOD eval显示NO：\n      Standard在MATH-500（30%）和HumanEval（37%）上也consistently outperform RASP（25%, 31%）。\n      Standard的OOD advantage（+5-6pp）甚至略大于in-distribution advantage（+7pp GSM8K），\n      说明Standard的SFT recovery建立了genuinely better reasoning ability而非memorization。\n      这是worst档对RASP最damaging的evidence之一——\n      即使在OOD evaluation下RASP也consistently inferior。\n      Recovery后的OOD performance大幅低于dense baseline\n      （MATH-500: 25-30% vs 52%），indicating significant OOD fragility for all pruned models。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 19: SFT OOD Evaluation\"\n        columns: [\"Model\", \"GSM8K (ID)\", \"MATH-500 (OOD)\", \"HumanEval (OOD)\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Dense\", \"76.4%\", \"52%\", \"58%\"]\n          - [\"Standard-20 + SFT\", \"63.5%\", \"30%\", \"37%\"]\n          - [\"RASP-20 + SFT\", \"55.3%\", \"25%\", \"31%\"]\n          - [\"Δ (Std−RASP)\", \"+8.2pp\", \"+5pp\", \"+6pp\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Grouped bar chart: ID vs OOD performance for SFT-recovered models\"\n    analysis: >\n      OOD eval eliminates memorization concern。Standard的recovery advantage is genuine。\n      论文中这应作为robustness evidence，\n      framed as：Standard pruning + SFT produces more generalizable recovery than RASP + SFT。\n      Implication：CKA-aware structure selection优化了wrong representational properties，\n      可能保留了task-specific circuits而非general reasoning scaffolding。\n```","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"7505ab55-e481-40a0-9dc6-f07ebf7a7c55","total_cost_usd":0.49598125,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":13279,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"output_tokens":15948,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":13279,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":15948,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"cache_creation_input_tokens":13279,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":13279},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":8237,"outputTokens":24,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.008357,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000},"claude-opus-4-6":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":15948,"cacheReadInputTokens":11841,"cacheCreationInputTokens":13279,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.48762425,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":64000}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"34055e94-6f0f-472f-954b-a801416e7ead"}
